-- title:
--   A subroutine's finite interaction transfers literally.
-- statement:
--   A subroutine's finite interaction transfers literally. When its terminal action is
--   reached the next phase runs at the same dispatch boundary. All costs count genuine calls.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.Inner.liftEpoch`, `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.Inner.liftGraph`, `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.Inner.liftRequest`.
